single-select-v2.content:
Usage



Server-side search

Put searchText in the search config to make search controlled. The component
renders that value, calls onSearchChange for every input change, and does not
filter items; the consumer supplies already-filtered API results.



Controlled mode is selected by the presence of search.searchText, including an
empty string. Omitting onSearchChange creates a read-only search input.
show: false hides the input but still disables internal filtering. Debouncing,
request cancellation, caching, and errors remain consumer responsibilities;
search loading is independent from pagination via hasMore/loadingComponent.

The controlled query persists when the menu closes and reopens. Clear it in
your own lifecycle handler only when that is the experience you want, for
example with onOpenChange={(open) => !open && setQuery('')}.

| SingleSelectV2 search field | Legacy SingleSelect equivalent |
| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| search.searchText           | searchText                     |
| search.onSearchChange       | onSearchChange                 |
| search.isSearchLoading      | isSearchLoading                |
| search.emptyStateText       | emptyStateText                 |

