single-select.content:
Usage



Server-side search

Pass searchText to make search controlled. In this mode, SingleSelect renders
that value, calls onSearchChange for every input change, and does not filter
items; supply the already-filtered API results yourself. Debouncing, request
cancellation, caching, and error handling remain consumer responsibilities.



Controlled mode is selected by the presence of searchText, including an empty
string. Omitting onSearchChange creates a read-only search input. Setting
enableSearch={false} hides the input but still disables internal filtering.
isSearchLoading describes search requests only; pagination continues to use
hasMore and loadingComponent.

The controlled query persists when the menu closes and reopens. Clear it from
your own UI only when that is the experience you want, for example from a
consumer-owned reset action that calls setQuery('').

| Legacy SingleSelect prop | SingleSelectV2 equivalent |
| -------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| searchText               | search.searchText         |
| onSearchChange           | search.onSearchChange     |
| isSearchLoading          | search.isSearchLoading    |
| emptyStateText           | search.emptyStateText     |

